WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:05.300
The best bloopers are the simple bloopers:
the ones where talented, glamorous movie stars

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.850
are supposed to be in character…and then
they burst into laughter.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.760
Maybe they flubbed a line, maybe they forgot
the line entirely, or maybe there's no reason

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.290
at all, and they just come down with a case
of the giggles.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:19.890
Here are a few actors who started laughing
during their scenes, and just couldn't stop.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.749
Eva Mendes - The Other Guys

00:00:21.749 --> 00:00:25.839
Will Ferrell keeps it pretty loose when filming
the silliest of his silly comedies.

00:00:25.839 --> 00:00:30.449
The Other Guys was directed by his longtime
writing partner Adam McKay, and both have

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:34.829
an extensive improv background, which means
Ferrell is strongly encouraged to riff while

00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:35.829
filming.

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:39.670
Unfortunately for his co-stars, they never
know quite what he's going to say or do, which

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:42.809
makes it very tough to keep their composure
and stay in character …

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:46.920
"I had to go to a specialist to get my hips
realigned."

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:53.420
"The doctor said it was similar to, uh, operating
on a German Shepard when they have, uh, hip

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.420
dysplasia."

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.390
"I can't do this right now!"

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.989
Brad Pitt - Moneyball

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:03.769
It's a serious, compelling movie that's surprisingly
riveting given it's mostly about a bunch of

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:07.942
people talking about baseball and doing math
to figure out which baseball players are the

00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:09.340
best investments.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.510
But all that dry office and locker room chatter
evidently made Brad Pitt go a little bit batty

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:14.800
on the set of Moneyball ...

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:20.040
"Now he's gonna do what's never been done."

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:25.830
"Now he's gonna do what's never been done."

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:30.040
"Now he's gonna do what he's never done.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.400
He's gonna round first, he's gonna take the
turn …"

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.020
Jimmy Fallon - Fever Pitch

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.270
He starred on Saturday Night Live for six
years and amassed an impressive legacy of

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.860
recurring characters and hilarious bits, but
Jimmy Fallon's probably best remembered for

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.890
his inability to keep a straight face through
sketches.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:56.840
When Fallon graduated from SNL into movies
in the 2000s, he couldn't drop his habit,

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.540
and apparently laughed a lot while shooting
the baseball comedy Fever Pitch ...

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.680
"Frankly, most of the men I've dated have
been poodles."

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.040
"I can't do it."

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.040
"I can't do it."

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.670
Paul Rudd and Leslie Mann - This is 40

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.920
Melissa McCarthy was a delightful surprise
in This is 40.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:23.340
She's a force of comic energy as she just
goes off on Rudd and Mann's characters, levying

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.450
a litany of hilarious improvised threats,
insults, and observations.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.310
McCarthy never cracks, but Rudd and Mann however,
can't control themselves ...

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.280
"And I'm glad your husband died.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.630
Because you're a f----ing a--hole.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.500
He probably killed himself."

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.380
Jonah Hill - This is the End

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.490
The end-of-the-world comedy This is the End
stars a bunch of Hollywood's top young actors

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:46.270
playing fictionalized versions of themselves.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:50.730
It's a crew of gifted comic performers with
agile improv comedy skills, including Jonah

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.730
Hill.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.980
A few mean-spirited lines Hill improvised
about co-star Michael Cera were so ridiculous

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.420
he couldn't keep a straight face ...

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:01.840
"Yeah, he goes and puts on the dress, and
like, like, he's weird, he competes in those

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:02.840
pageants and shit."

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:03.840
"Wait.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.840
So he …"

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:05.840
"Yeah, he pretends to be a kid …"

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.590
"Dude never met a condom."

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:08.590
"You're f---ing with me."

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:09.670
"For real, dude, honestly, he probably has
some s---.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.260
I know he has AIDS, actually."

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.260
"What?!"

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.620
Johnny Depp - Pirates of the Caribbean

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.319
Getting paid millions to dress up like a pirate?

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:21.140
That's just life for Johnny Depp, who has
starred as Captain Jack Sparrow in multiple

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.850
Pirates of the Caribbean blockbusters.

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:27.020
He's clearly delighted to get to play a high-seas
buccaneer—because he has such a good time

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.700
he just can't quit laughing on the set ...

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.460
"You knew this."

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.140
"I did not."

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.380
"You knew this."

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.180
"I did not!"

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.600
"Not for me.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.060
For my father."

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.500
"It's gonna be okay.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.360
We're gonna keep going."

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.360
"Cut it!"

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.290
Margot Robbie - Suicide Squad

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.380
There was a lot to laugh at during the filming
of Suicide Squad.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:57.580
It's one of the most over-the-top comic book
movies ever made, with multiple over-the-top

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:02.540
villains in over-the-top costumes with over-the-top
personalities vying for screen time.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:07.820
Margot Robbie played Harley Quinn, a protégé
of the Joker, and Robbie, befitting the character,

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.180
was quick to laugh on set...

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.080
"Jesus!"

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:12.660
"Sorry."

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.840
"If I could see my actual reflection, it would
have …"

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.759
Mila Kunis - Bad Moms

00:04:21.759 --> 00:04:27.289
The cast of this 2016 comedy was stacked with
hilarious people, and star Mila Kunis is no

00:04:27.289 --> 00:04:31.319
slouch either, with eight years of That '70s
Show on her resume.

00:04:31.319 --> 00:04:35.759
The laughter flowed fast and furious for Kunis
while making the ensemble comedy — it didn't

00:04:35.759 --> 00:04:37.620
take much for her to get the giggles …

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.180
"I've been watching Extra.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.270
You gotta check out Brad Pitt's new haircut.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:43.260
Tight."

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.120
"This chicken sucks."

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.189
"Then don't eat it."

00:04:47.189 --> 00:04:48.560
"I'll eat it.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.060
Give it to me.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.420
It's fine."

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.300
Thanks for watching!

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.120
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.680
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

